  "live_records": {
    "q-162673": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162673",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{t+1} \\\\ {e}^{t} \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{t+1}$ is $t\\in [-1,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${e}^{t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $2t$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242901/assets/3f1ca1c3d6ffd56fe0686ee209c967775b5daf09a99e80a3f38ad0a56f4424ce.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in [-1,\\infty ).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
