    "q-162654": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162654",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=⟨\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,8s,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+2)⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $8s$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+2)$ is $s\\in (-2,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242901/assets/39aa3fde0371988849572ce6f92a7e9994e4756db4aafd6f82dc7c86aa321dc1.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in (-2,\\infty ).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
