    "q-162646": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162646",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+({t}^{3}+1)\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n2t=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{3}+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
