    "q-162634": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162634",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)={t}^{4}\\,i+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component ${t}^{4}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
