    "q-162635": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162635",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)={e}^{1-t}\\,i+(2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1)\\,j+t\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component ${e}^{1-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
